---
source: crates/pogo-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Measure current and voltage with the INA226

Usage: pogo power measure [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --duration <DURATION>
          [default: 5s]

      --interval <INTERVAL>
          [default: 1ms]

      --out <FILE>
          Also write raw samples to a CSV file

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -d, --device <SELECTOR>
          Target device: alias, USB serial, port, or "auto"

      --probe <SELECTOR>
          Probe device [default: "probe" alias, else auto]

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format [default: human]
          
          [env: POGO_FORMAT=]
          [possible values: human, json, jsonl]

      --config <PATH>
          Config file
          
          [env: POGO_CONFIG=]

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Overall deadline for this command, e.g. 500ms, 10s, 2m

      --wait-lock <DURATION>
          Wait for a busy device instead of failing

      --dry-run
          Describe what a mutating command would do; change nothing

  -v, --verbose...
          More logs on stderr (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on stderr

      --no-color
          Disable colors

Requires the probe and an INA226. The target must be powered through the shunt, not USB.

Examples:
  pogo power measure --duration 10s -f json
  pogo power measure --interval 2ms --out samples.csv

Exit codes: 0 ok, 3 probe not found, 6 probe I/O or protocol

JSON data: { duration_ms, samples, dropped, current_ma: { avg, min, max, p50, p95 },
bus_voltage_v: { avg, min, max }, energy_mj, csv_path }
